TITLE:: RLWalk
summary:: A walk on chords: a start and a word, with its voices
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLChordContext, Classes/RLMorphism, Classes/RLVoiceLeading, Classes/RLTransform, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A walk is a strong::start:: chord in a context and a strong::word::, the list of its steps strong::in the order they are taken::. A step is the Symbol of one of the context's transformations (code::\P::, code::\L::, code::\R::, or a name it defines), or an link::Classes/RLTransform::.

The same word can be read in any context that knows its names: link::#-inContext:: carries a walk from 12 equal steps to 19, or to the just lattice, where a walk that closed may not close any more. link::#-drift:: says where a walk ends from where it started: nothing when it closes, a comma for the lift of a closed walk (link::Classes/RLMorphism::).

A walk also has voices: link::#-voices:: plays it from a voicing, each chord reached by the least motion from the one before (link::Classes/RLVoiceLeading::), and link::#-voiceDrift:: says how far each voice is from where it began once the walk is over. A walk can close on its chords and not on its voices.

code::
~ctx = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12)));
~pump = RLWalk(~ctx, ~ctx.space.major(0), [\R, \L, \R, \P, \R, \L, \R, \L]);
~pump.chords;                        // C major, A minor, F major, D minor, D major, B minor, G major, E minor, C major
~pump.isClosed;                      // true
~pump.voices([60, 64, 67]).last;     // [64, 67, 72]: back on C major, one inversion higher
~pump.voiceDrift([60, 64, 67]);      // [4, 3, 5]

~just = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLJust([3, 5])));
~lifted = ~pump.inContext(~just);    // the same word from 1/1 major
~lifted.isClosed;                    // false
~lifted.drift;                       // [-4, 1]
~lifted.driftCents;                  // -21.5: a syntonic comma down

RLWalk.cycle(~ctx, ~ctx.space.major(0), [\P, \L]).chords;    // the hexatonic cycle, 6 steps
~e19 = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(19)));
RLWalk.cycle(~e19, ~e19.space.major(0), [\P, \L]).size;      // 38 steps in 19
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: context
argument:: start
A chord of the context.
argument:: word
An Array of Symbols or RLTransforms, in time order.

METHOD:: cycle
A word repeated until the walk is back on its start; nil when it has not closed after strong::maxRepeats::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: context
METHOD:: start
METHOD:: word

METHOD:: transforms
The steps as RLTransforms.

METHOD:: chords
The chords met, the start first: one more than the word has steps.

METHOD:: end
The last chord.

METHOD:: size
The number of steps.

METHOD:: isClosed
Whether the walk ends on its start.

METHOD:: composed
The whole walk as one transformation.

METHOD:: drift
The interval from the start's root to the end's, a pitch class of the system, when the two chords have the same type; nil when they differ.

METHOD:: driftCents
The drift in cents, or nil.

METHOD:: inContext
The same word in another context.
argument:: other
argument:: from
A chord of the other context; its base chord of the start's type when nil.

METHOD:: repeated
The word n times.

METHOD:: ++
One walk's word after another's, from this walk's start.

SUBSECTION:: Voices

METHOD:: voices
The voicings of its chords, one Array of pitches per chord.
argument:: from
A voicing of the start chord (anything else is an Error); close position at the origin when nil.

METHOD:: voiceDrift
How far each voice ends from where it began, as pitch intervals (steps in RLEDO).

METHOD:: voiceCents
The motion of the voices at each step, in cents.
argument:: from
argument:: measure
code::\l1::, code::\l2:: or code::\linf:: (link::Classes/RLVoiceLeading#*cents::).

METHOD:: freqs
The voicings as frequencies.
argument:: from
argument:: base
The frequency of the origin.

METHOD:: asPattern
The frequencies as a link::Classes/Pseq:: of chords.
argument:: from
argument:: base
argument:: repeats

EXAMPLES::
code::
// one walk, the same voices, in three tunings (with a server running)
(
~word = [\R, \L, \R, \P, \R, \L, \R, \L];
~play = { |system|
	var ctx = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(system));
	Pbind(\freq, RLWalk(ctx, ctx.space.major, ~word).asPattern(nil, 220), \dur, 1, \legato, 1).play;
};
)
~play.(RLEDO(12));
~play.(RLEDO(19));
~play.(RLJust([3, 5]));     // ends a syntonic comma below where it began
::
